":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.7.dev [0b3dc97], 4.6.stable.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9174) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-12700H (20 threads) - 15.69 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe 3D grid snap precision is limited to 3 decimal places (0.001). However, the \"position\" property of a Node3D supports 4 decimal places (0.0001) in the inspector tab. This is inconsistent.\n\n| Grid Snap     | Inspector     |\n| ------------- | ------------- |\n| <img width=\"155\" height=\"182\" alt=\"Image 2026-04-18_22-30-15\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9a1a1a19-61d5-462f-af3d-7d63e0b859b3\" /> | <img width=\"245\" height=\"444\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/81e50a78-6b21-4634-baa5-36715223a759\" /> |\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open a 3D scene.\n2. In the scene toolbar, click \"Transform > Configure Snap\", and set \"Translate Snap\" to \"0.0009\".\n3. Notice that it gets rounded to \"0.001\" instead.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscr